# SHA256 manifest for EigenLabs/Qwen3.8-27B-MTP-bf16.
# Revision: 26a328e070875b0314d652a039b6b59902690f03
# Format: <sha256> <byte_count> <relative_path>
#
# GENERATED FROM THE PUBLISHED HEAD REPOSITORY 2026-08-14, replacing the 3.6
# head's records this file carried as a worked example while the upload was
# outstanding. The head was extracted from the official bf16 base
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B @ 1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0 and published at
# the revision above.
#
# THE PUBLISHED TREE IS FOUR FILES, and the reason is the LOADER, not the
# upload. The first publish carried only model.safetensors plus the
# `.gitattributes` Hugging Face generates for every repository, on the reasoning
# that the head merges into the target's tree under the `mtp.` prefix at load
# and carries no independent tokenizer. That reasoning was right about the
# tokenizer and wrong about the rest: Qwen36MTPHeadAttachment.verifyHeadTree
# REQUIRES `model.safetensors.index.json` and `config.json` in the head
# directory and refuses the load without them. It reads the index to assert the
# head names exactly 15 BARE tensors -- a pre-merged, already-`mtp.`-prefixed
# tree is refused rather than accommodated -- and it reads the config to assert
# the head belongs to the same architecture family and declares the single MTP
# layer the backbone's `mtp_num_hidden_layers: 1` promises. Neither file is a
# load INPUT (the model is built from the backbone's config); both are
# compatibility assertions the head cannot be verified without. So the head
# repository grew to four files at revision 26a328e0 and the manifest, the
# workflow shape pins and the contract fixture moved with it. There are still no
# tokenizer files, and there never will be.
#
# `.gitattributes` IS PINNED. The ranked workflow's `verify_cache` runs a
# strict flat inventory check in BOTH directions and rejects any file in the
# cache that the manifest does not name; a stock `snapshot_download` stages it,
# so omitting the record would not keep a git plumbing file out of the pins, it
# would just fail the run (run 31665285024 died on exactly that).
#
# THE ON-BOX STAGING DIRECTORY IS NOT THIS TREE. The eight-file layout that
# ~/qwen38-mtp-head held on the ai-server is box-local extraction scratch; what
# this manifest pins, and what MLXFAST_QWEN_MTP_HEAD_DIR must contain
# file-for-file, is the PUBLISHED repository above.
#
# The whole-manifest shape pins move with this body, in this commit:
#
#   MLXFAST_QWEN_MTP_HEAD_MANIFEST_RECORDS: 4
#   MLXFAST_QWEN_MTP_HEAD_MANIFEST_BYTES:   849406438
#
# and so do the contract fixture's mtp_head.manifest_sha256 and
# mtp_head.expected_total_bytes.
#
# THE LAST PINNED HEAD, kept as provenance rather than as a template now that
# real records exist, was mlx-community/Qwen3.6-27B-MTP-4bit @
# 83795d546e9d328160e593fb0bf10b2bf2fe637e: 8 records, 258490810 bytes, and a
# 31-tensor index, because that head was 4-bit group-64 and its 8 matrices
# appeared as weight/scales/biases triples alongside 7 norms. The 3.8 head is
# bf16, so the same 8 matrices are 8 entries and 8 + 7 = 15.
